"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vz0ul","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-06T15:23:11Z","updated_at":"2025-06-06T15:23:33Z","body":"For future reference, this is not a bug. The Mobile rendering method uses RGB10A2 (with a 2.0 exposure multiplier), so colors are naturally less precise than in Forward+ which uses RGBAH, or even Compatibility which uses RGB8 but in sRGB space and with a 1.0 exposure multiplier.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4193 largely addresses this issue by performing debanding at a material level, at the cost of slightly visible noise. See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7336.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2949598117/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]